================================================================================
PORTFOLIO NI PRINCE - LOCAL SETUP & INSTALLATION GUIDE
================================================================================

PREREQUISITES:
- Python 3.12 or higher installed on your system
- Git installed on your system

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP-BY-STEP LOCAL INSTRUCTIONS:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. CLONE THE REPOSITORY
   Open your terminal (PowerShell, Command Prompt, or Bash) and clone the repo:
   git clone https://github.com/PrinceU-8/PORTFOLIO.git
   cd PORTFOLIO

2. CREATE AND ACTIVATE A VIRTUAL ENVIRONMENT
   Windows (PowerShell):
     python -m venv .venv
     .venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
     (Note: If script execution is restricted on Windows, first run:
      Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass)

   macOS / Linux:
     python3 -m venv .venv
     source .venv/bin/activate

3. INSTALL PROJECT DEPENDENCIES
   Upgrade pip and install all required packages from requirements.txt:
   python -m pip install --upgrade pip
   pip install -r requirements.txt

4. ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
   Copy the example environment file into a local .env file in the root directory:
   Windows:
     copy .env.example .env
   macOS / Linux:
     cp .env.example .env

   Ensure your .env file contains the following values:
   SECRET_KEY=django-insecure-local-dev-key-change-this-in-production
   DEBUG=True
   ALLOWED_HOSTS=127.0.0.1,localhost

5. INITIALIZE THE DATABASE (MIGRATIONS)
   Run the initial schema migrations to set up your local SQLite database:
   python manage.py migrate

6. CREATE A SUPERUSER ACCOUNT
   To log in to the moderation dashboard and activate the superuser portal:
   python manage.py createsuperuser
   Follow the prompts to configure your username, email, and password.

7. START THE LOCAL DEVELOPMENT SERVER
   python manage.py runserver

   Open your browser and navigate to:
   http://127.0.0.1:8000/

(IMPORTANT DETAILS)
Personal details is not available at fresh install, they are only configured 
in Django admin also, thus, input details there. (Quiz did not require to be
to configure it in the admin dashboard. Coudln't implement it now due to time 
constraints.)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CORE APPLICATION ROUTES:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- /              : Landing / Hero page
- /about/        : Personal bio, experience timeline, and interactive skill cluster
- /works/        : Project portfolio and project detail cards
- /testimony/    : Client testimonials display and testimonial submission form
- /contact/      : Direct contact and inquiry submission form
- /admin-login/  : Administrator sign-in portal
- /dashboard/    : Superuser management hub (CRUD for projects and testimonials)
- /logout/       : Terminate administrator session

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WEBSITE QUIRKS & EASTER EGGS:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- DYNAMIC REVERSIBLE NAVBAR:
  The navigation header automatically isolates the active view in the center 
  with a persistent underline, while filtering out duplicate links from the 
  right-hand navigation cluster dynamically across all routes.

- FLOATING CAPYBARA DASHBOARD PORTAL:
  A fixed, hovering capybara icon appears at the bottom-right of every page, 
  strictly rendered for authenticated superusers as a direct shortcut to the 
  administrative dashboard.

- INTERACTIVE PHYSICS-STYLE SKILL CLUSTER:
  The About page contains an animated, floating bubble cluster connected by 
  dynamic vector line geometry that highlights technical proficiencies.

- SECRET INPUT:
  To Access login you must input a set of actions
  (@home click
  lastname
  firstname
  middlename
  then the squares in:
  1,4,3,2 order).

